 </success_criteria>
 
-## Universal Enforcement (v1.5)
-
-The central gate is `rig-loop dispatch_hook`, above loop-specific logic and
-active even when no loop run exists. Claude, Codex, Hermes, OMP, and Prime Agent
-must route mutation-class pre-tool calls through it. Protected roots come only
-from `~/.rig/d85/enforcement.json`; a `write`, `edit`, `bash`/`shell`,
-`apply_patch`, or equivalent mutation touching an exact path beneath one of
-those roots requires a current signed admission for that path and session.
+## Current scope: solution and app build quality
+
+Mike corrected the policy on 2026-09-11. D85 requires at least 85% deterministic source-derived operations in solution, application, and durable-system builds, together with RIG Lattice routing and artifact proof. Ordinary startup, research, diagnostics, memory capture, Python, shell commands, and authorized edits do not require D85 admission. Do not block those operations because of their path or verb. Other authorization rules remain independent.
+
+Use `rig-lattice route` and `rig-lattice bms score` before edits. Submit the validated routing context with the build checklist. Certification recomputes `score_process`, requires REALIZED_PASS, and binds the live score to the source inventory. A submitted `d85_realized_pass` is not evidence by itself. Run `rig-lattice audit` for the artifact, retain the audit in the ProofPacket, and verify the build certificate before promotion.
+
+Solution and app build loop specs must declare a final `d85_certified` gate with the build record, certificate, and root paths. It is a direct verifier call and is non-forceable at completion and sealing. Ordinary loop operation continues. Missing or failing evidence blocks certification, not further repair work. Old build records without Lattice evidence must be migrated and recertified.
+
+## Explicit legacy admission and launcher APIs
+
+The following admission ceremony, sandbox launcher, estate checks, and recovery procedures apply only when an operator explicitly chooses those legacy APIs. They are retained for existing consumers. They are not installed as a universal D85 pre-tool requirement. The central `rig-loop dispatch_hook` does not call the legacy `hook_check` for ordinary tools.
 
 ### Admission ceremony
 
diff --git a/capabilities/skills/rig-determinism-85/authority/doctrine.md b/capabilities/skills/rig-determinism-85/authority/doctrine.md
